<title>UK: Shell Rotterdam cuts crude runs a further 5 pct.</title>
<headline>Shell Rotterdam cuts crude runs a further 5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shell's Rotterdam refinery will cut crude oil runs a further five percent from Wednesday, adding to cuts of 12 to 15 percent made last week, trade sources said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>The cuts will be on low sulphur crude runs only and will be the equivalent of about 22,000 barrels per day (bpd) or some 12 percent of current low sulphur throughput.</p>
<p>Last week sources said Shell was cutting nearly 50,000 bpd of crude runs without specifying whether they were from low or high sulphur crudes.</p>
<p>The latest cuts are due to be implemented on Wednesday and will continue for &quot;at least two weeks&quot;, the source said.</p>
<p>The Shell Rotterdam refinery has a nameplate capacity of 374,000 bpd.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 4984</p>
